A candidate highlighted
description: the dropdown_armed state
- >
  ArrowDown/Up (or hover) armed a row; arrows cycle with wraparound. Enter, Tab or a click takes
  it - the cell's text becomes the candidate's segment spelling. A MIDDLE cell keeps its tail (the
  query re-filters); the LAST cell opens a fresh append cell after it, ready for the next step
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`down_arrow`', '', '`dropdown_armed` (stays)']
  - ['`up_arrow`', '', '`dropdown_armed` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', '', '[cell_editing](*::server:query-editor:cell_editing)']
  - ['`tab`', '', '[cell_editing](*::server:query-editor:cell_editing)']
  - ['`click_candidate`', '', '[cell_editing](*::server:query-editor:cell_editing)']
  - ['`escape`', '', '[dropdown_open](*::server:query-editor:dropdown_open)']
  - ['`alphanumeric`', '', '[dropdown_open](*::server:query-editor:dropdown_open)']
